   "source": [
    "# Five-way golf-club CNN\n",
    "\n",
    "Fine-tune a pretrained ResNet-50 to classify a club-head image as Driver, Wood, Hybrid, Iron, or Wedge. The notebook keeps related images from the same product together, applies identical resize and normalization to every split, and applies augmentation only to training images.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Deployment context:** this model must identify the club in a golfer's hands *before* the swing starts (the address/setup frame), not mid-swing. Training data is still catalog-style photos of isolated club heads, so real address-position frames (grass/background clutter, camera angle, partial occlusion by the grip and hands) are a real domain shift from this reference set. Treat catalog test accuracy as an upper bound, not a guarantee of field accuracy, and validate with a small held-out set of real address-position captures before trusting production confidence thresholds.\n",
    "\n",
    "Run the cells from top to bottom. Training **requires a CUDA GPU** \u2014 the notebook raises immediately if none is available rather than silently falling back to CPU or MPS. The best checkpoint (selected by validation accuracy, tie-broken by validation loss, matching the model-selection logic in Section 5) is saved to `models/trained/club_type_5way.pt`. ResNet-50 uses a 35-epoch maximum with early stopping, 288-pixel inputs, late-stage fine-tuning, and class-stratified group splits.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Data note:** `product_group()` collapses filename suffixes such as `_aug1`, `_zoom`, or `_flip` so augmented variants of one source photo stay in the same split. Newly added files named with a bare `aug_NNNNN` prefix have no traceable source stem, so they are treated as their own independent groups. If those files are offline-augmented duplicates of a photo that also appears elsewhere in this dataset, confirm that with whoever generated them \u2014 filename-only grouping cannot detect that case, and it would leak near-duplicate images across train/validation/test and inflate reported accuracy.\n",
    "\n",
    "Rerun the notebook before judging a new configuration; any saved cell outputs are only illustrative results from an earlier run. The reference set is useful for validating the workflow, but add varied real-world club-head photos (ideally address-position frames) before relying on the model in production."
